---
title: iMessage Bridge and Conversation Loop
---
flowchart LR
    Sender([Allowlisted sender's phone]) <--> Messages

    subgraph Mac[Mac — operator's trust zone]
        Messages[Messages.app<br/>sends as the pinned account id]
        ChatDB[(chat.db<br/>opened read-only, WAL-aware)]
        Bridge[Bridge MCP server<br/>x-anios-bridge-token middleware<br/>allowlist plus grants decide who is heard]
        Filter[Stranger and group-chat filter<br/>plus 3s settle window<br/>bodies never leave the process or logs]
        Bridge -->|osascript argv only<br/>never interpolated| Messages
        ChatDB --> Filter --> Bridge
    end

    subgraph AniOS[AniOS — backend trust zone]
        Worker[imessage worker<br/>owns the nanosecond cursor<br/>guid dedup across restarts]
        Conversation[ConversationService<br/>full pipeline including memory writes<br/>an explicit operator decision]
        Channel[MessagesAppChannel<br/>arguments screened by<br/>OutboundPrivacyPolicy]
    end

    Worker -->|read_messages since_ns<br/>IMESSAGE_BRIDGE_READ_INCOMING gate| Bridge
    Bridge -->|allowlisted 1:1 bodies only<br/>sender normalized, reply_to canonical| Worker
    Worker --> Conversation
    Conversation --> Channel
    Channel -->|send_imessage to reply_to| Bridge

    Identity[The sending identity is whatever Apple ID<br/>Messages is signed into — pin it with<br/>IMESSAGE_BRIDGE_ACCOUNT_ID or the tie breaks wrong]
    Identity -.-> Messages

